{"run_id": "run-20260831T011829Z", "cell_id": "ontology.g27de-d1-instances-of.engine-briefed.haiku-4.5", "domain": "ontology", "task_id": "g27de-d1-instances-of", "question_class": "recursion", "engine_expected_to_help": true, "track": "in-context", "difficulty": 1, "arm": "engine-briefed", "strength": "haiku-4.5", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "ablated": null, "verdict": "correct", "missing": 0, "extra": 0, "truth_size": 4, "answer_raw": "o27de00009\no27de00010\no27de00011\no27de00013\n", "unparseable_reason": null, "first_program": "% Import the data\nimport \"instance.csv\" as instance.\nimport \"subclass.csv\" as subclass.\n\n% A class is a subclass of itself\nis_subclass(C, C).\n\n% Transitively, if C1 is a subclass of C2, and C2 is a subclass of C3, then C1 is a subclass of C3\nis_subclass(C1, C3) :- subclass(C1, C2), is_subclass(C2, C3).\n\n% An instance is an instance of a class if:\n% 1. It's directly listed as an instance of that class, or\n% 2. It's an instance of a class that is a subclass of that class\ninstance_of(I, C) :- instance(I, C).\ninstance_of(I, C) :- instance(I, C2), is_subclass(C2, C).\n\n% Query: find all instances of k27de004 (including instances of classes that are subclasses of k27de004)\nanswer(I) :- instance_of(I, k27de004).\n", "first_program_turn": 4, "malformed_calls": 0, "truncated_completions": 0, "empty_replies": 0, "finished_without_answer": false, "signals": {"engine_use": "answered-from", "wrote_program": true, "ran_engine": true, "engine_calls": 3, "searches_after_engine": 0, "searches_total": 0, "rounds": 3}, "input_tokens": 73, "output_tokens": 4683, "cache_read_tokens": 171732, "cache_creation_tokens": 24309, "cost_usd": 0.09488020000000003, "wall_seconds": 39.92, "turns": 10, "denials": [], "error": null, "recorded_at": "2026-08-31T01:29:37.548801+00:00"}
